{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall bring them and plant them.</b> The mountain of Your inheritance is understood. As in וישמחו כל חוסי בך לעולם ירננו ותסך עלימו." "<b>You shall bring them and plant them.</b> Rashi explained that he prophesied that he would not enter the land. And one should not object from this to תראה, nor to the thirty-one kings that Rashi discussed at the end of the portion of Shemot, for the Holy One, blessed be He, did not say this to him; rather, we derive it. Even so, from מנוסעים אנחנו in the portion of BeHa'alotekha, he included himself with them." "<b>And plant them.</b> A prolonged standing, as if planted. And similarly: בהר מרום ישראל אשתלנו." "<b>The sanctuary of YHWH.</b> With alef-dalet."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:03.063647130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}